      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "6b7b05e27104ef71c4ae707d69bcc7e9",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"salt-and-pepper-noise-min-max-and-median-filters\">Salt-and-pepper noise: min, max, and median filters</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This animation demonstrates how neighborhood filters act on an\n8-bit grayscale image contaminated with <strong>salt-and-pepper noise</strong>.</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Min filter</strong> replaces the center pixel by the minimum value in\n  the neighborhood. It is therefore especially effective against\n  <strong>salt noise</strong> (bright, value 255).</li>\n<li><strong>Max filter</strong> replaces the center pixel by the maximum value in\n  the neighborhood. It is especially effective against\n  <strong>pepper noise</strong> (dark, value 0).</li>\n<li><strong>Median filter</strong> replaces the center pixel by the median of the\n  neighborhood. It can suppress <strong>both salt and pepper noise</strong> while\n  preserving edges better than min/max filtering.</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The red square indicates the current filter neighborhood. The right\npanel is revealed progressively in raster-scan order.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
