          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"interpretation\">Interpretation</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A <strong>3x3 median filter</strong> sorts the\nneighborhood values and chooses the middle one.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Isolated 0 and 255 values therefore have little influence unless they\noccupy a large fraction of the neighborhood. This makes median\nfiltering particularly suitable for <strong>salt-and-pepper noise</strong>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Increasing the kernel size suppresses larger noise clusters, but also\nremoves progressively more fine image detail.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
